From df1979e68d50229a47e5113cd06a8d15dd34c753 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kunal Jha <kunal.jha3@in.ey.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 08:34:50 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] test(api): every route for every role against a real
 database, and the defects it found

FRONTEND_HARDENING.md section 2, partial. Stopped mid-section on request; what
is here is complete and green, and what is not started is named below.

tests/e2e/test_api_contract.py calls all 56 routes as admin, strategist, block
and anonymously against the loaded dev database and asserts the status matches
the role dependency the handler declares - 200 when admitted, 403 when not,
401 anonymous, and never 500. The route list is derived from the app and a
route with no entry in the call table fails the test, so an endpoint cannot be
added without saying how to call it. It also covers block-role AC scoping, an
AC with nothing loaded, the legacy 308s, and the review queue end to end.

tests/test_api_topology.py proves routes are registered and
tests/test_api_sql_relations.py proves their SQL names relations that exist.
Neither executes a query, which is why five endpoints have been returning 500
since 0015_metrics.sql rebuilt the metric views:

- N15 `votes_counted` -> `votes_polled` and `total_valid` -> `valid_votes`,
      renamed by 0015 and never carried through. Fixed in api/routers/data.py,
      analytics/metrics.sql and web/src/pages/Results.tsx.
- N20 POST /admin/crosswalk inserted into booth_crosswalk without ac_id, so
      the only manual override an admin has over the crosswalk never worked.
- N21 GET /caste selected caste_estimate.matched_pct and .method_version,
      neither of which existed. The Caste page could never have loaded.
- N22 write_surname_estimates - the writer parse_roll actually calls - still
      normalised over matched tokens and wrote no residual, so a booth where
      the dictionary placed 40% of names reported shares summing to 100%.
      C14 was fixed in the computation and not in the writer. refresh() also
      inserted without ac_id. Both now write shares over the electorate, an
      explicit UNMATCHED row, matched_pct and method_version.
- N19 review-queue writers set no ac_id, and the admin route filters on it, so
      every Form 20 row the LLD 4.2 gate rejected landed in a queue the Admin
      page could not show. No conflict target either, so a re-run raised
      instead of updating.
- N17 review_queue.kind had no 'form20_column', so the failure path of the C1
      fix would itself have failed.

0018_queue_kinds_and_caste_columns.sql carries the schema half: the kind list
the code actually writes, ac_id NOT NULL on review_queue, and
caste_estimate.matched_pct / .method_version.

scripts/endpoint_inventory.py generates docs/ENDPOINTS.md - 70 routes against
30 frontend call sites - and flags calls to routes that do not exist, routes no
page calls, parameters a page sends that a route rejects, and routes with no
explicit response model. `--check` fails when the document is stale. It found 0
orphan calls and 0 bad parameters once the scanner handled ac.path() and nested
template literals; an earlier scanner in this repo reported false misses from
exactly that.

Not done, and not started: explicit pydantic response models (5 routes still
return a bare dict), generating frontend types from the OpenAPI schema, and
validating the fixtures against the response models. GET /acs/{ac}/summary and
GET /acs/{ac}/booths/{uid}/card still 500 on further stale column names and are
recorded as strict xfail against N15, so a fix forces the marker's removal
rather than leaving the suite red or the defect hidden.

Gates: pytest 756 passed, 1 skipped; tests/e2e 359 passed, 8 skipped,
7 xfailed; ruff clean; lint_sql clean; endpoint_inventory --check clean;
npm run build clean; no secret staged. NEXT_STEPS.md left untracked - not mine.

